    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $p$ is an inner fibration, the induced map $\widetilde{\phi }: \calC _{/X} \rightarrow \calD _{/p(X)} \times _{\calD } \calC $ is a right fibration by Proposition <a href="/tag/EEE6AE" data-tag="EEE6AE">2.1.2.1</a>. We note that $\phi $ is obtained from $\widetilde{\phi }$ by restricting to the fiber over the vertex $Y$ of $\calC $. Thus $\phi $ is a right fibration; since the target of $\phi $ is a Kan complex, $\phi $ is a Kan fibration by Lemma <a href="/tag/B732E8" data-tag="B732E8">2.1.3.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
